#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:2
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "Primeros pasos"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:4
msgid ""
"To get started with VMware, simply start by adding a Cloud in the "
"``Infrastructure > Clouds`` section."
msgstr ""
"To get started con VMware, simply start by adding un Cloud in el "
"``Infrastructure > Clouds`` sección."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:6
msgid ""
"To start adding a VMware cloud there will be some things you will need:"
msgstr ""
"To start adding un VMware cloud allí será be algunos things you será need:"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:8
msgid "vCenter API Url"
msgstr "vCenter API Url"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:9
msgid ""
"Typically this is the url to the vCenter web client with a ``/sdk`` in the "
"path"
msgstr ""
"Típicamente este es el url to el vCenter web client con un ``/sdk`` in el "
"ruta"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:11
msgid "Username/Password"
msgstr "Username/Password"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:11
msgid ""
"A set of credentials with high level access to VMware (ensure the account "
"has Datacenter level access)"
msgstr ""
"A set of credentials con high level acceso to VMware (ensure el cuenta tiene"
" Datacenter level acceso)"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:13
msgid ""
"Once these fields are entered, some selections will start pre-populating. A "
"cloud integration is scoped to a specific data center, and can optionally be"
" scoped down to a single cluster or even a single resource pool. If the drop"
" downs do not populate, please verify the api url is resolvable, morpheus "
"has access to vCenter on 443, and the provided credentials are correct and "
"the user has sufficient permissions."
msgstr ""
"Once estos campos son entered, algunos selections será start pre-populating."
" A cloud integration es scoped to un específico datos center, y puede "
"opcionalmente be scoped down to un único cluster o incluso un único recurso "
"pool. If el drop downs no populate, please verify el api url es resolvable, "
"morpheus tiene acceso to vCenter on 443, y el provided credentials son "
"correct y el usuario tiene sufficient permisos."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:15
msgid ""
"Another cool feature provided with the cloud integration is optional "
"`Resource Pool` scoping. One can choose to allow the cloud to provision into"
" All Resource Pools or a singular Resource Pool. When choosing `All`, these "
"Resource Pools can be managed from a sub-account and visibility perspective "
"via the Cloud Detail page (multi-tenancy)."
msgstr ""
"Another cool característica provided con la nube integration es opcional "
"`Resource Pool` scoping. One puede choose to allow la nube to provision en "
"All Resource Pools o un singular Resource Pool. When choosing `All`, estos "
"Resource Pools se puede administrar desde un sub-cuenta y visibility "
"perspective via el Cloud Detail página (multi-tenancy)."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:17
msgid ""
"The VMware cloud integration provides a few additional options including "
"allowing users to make host selections or keeping that aspect hidden such "
"that the best host is automatically chosen for the requested provision."
msgstr ""
"The VMware cloud integration provides un few adicional opciones including "
"allowing users to make host selections o keeping que aspect hidden such que "
"el best host es automáticamente chosen para el requested provision."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:19
msgid ""
"The *RPC Mode* feature can be configured to allow |morpheus| to install its "
"agent on the Guest operating system via either SSH/WinRM or Vmware Tools "
"Guest Process feature. The VMware tools Guest Execution API can be tricky so"
" it is recommended to use SSH/WinRM if possible. However, if it is not "
"possible for the Appliance to have outbound access to all networks in which "
"VMs are being provisioned to the SSH/WinRM ports (22, 5985 respectively) "
"then Guest Execution is the only option."
msgstr ""
"The *RPC Mode* característica se puede configurar to allow |morpheus| to "
"install its agent on el Guest operating sistema via either SSH/WinRM o "
"Vmware Tools Guest Process característica. The VMware tools Guest Execution "
"API puede be tricky so it es recomendado to use SSH/WinRM if possible. Sin "
"embargo, if it no es possible para el Appliance to tienen outbound acceso to"
" todos networks in cual VMs son being provisioned to el SSH/WinRM ports (22,"
" 5985 respectively) entonces Guest Execution es el solo opción."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:21
msgid ""
"The `Use VNC` console option on the VMware cloud requires special "
"configuration on each ESXI host but allowed hypervisor level remote console "
"support. (See the Advanced Section for details)"
msgstr ""
"The `Use VNC` console opción on el VMware cloud requires special "
"configuración on cada ESXI host pero allowed hypervisor level remoto console"
" support. (See el Advanced Section para detalles)"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:23
msgid ""
"When following this add cloud wizard an option will be presented to create a"
" group or add to an existing group. These groups can be given provisioning "
"permission via  role based access control. It is normally recommended that "
"groups are organized such that one cloud exists in one group unless the "
"networks are setup such that internal routing is possible between the "
"clouds. This is very useful for bursting, or hybrid cloud configurations."
msgstr ""
"When following este add cloud wizard un opción será be presented to create "
"un grupo o add to un existente group. These groups puede be given "
"provisioning permiso via  role based acceso control. It es normalmente "
"recomendado que groups son organized such que one cloud exists in one group "
"unless la reds son setup such que interno routing es possible entre la "
"nubes. This es muy useful para bursting, o hybrid cloud configurations."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:26
msgid "Windows Provisioning Tips"
msgstr "Windows Provisioning Tips"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:28
msgid ""
"By default when provisioning windows templates, |morpheus| performs guest "
"customizations which initiates a sysprep. This resets the Administrator user"
" and password. |morpheus| will set the Administrator password from "
"|AdmSetPro| > Windows Settings > Password."
msgstr ""
"By predeterminado cuando provisioning windows templates, |morpheus| performs"
" guest customizations cual initiates un sysprep. This resets el "
"Administrator user y contraseña. |morpheus| será set el Administrator "
"contraseña desde |AdmSetPro| > Windows Settings > Password."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:30
msgid ""
"Users can also set the username on an image as Administrator and enter a "
"different password if unique passwords are required per image."
msgstr ""
"Users puede también set el usuarioname on un image as Administrator y enter "
"un diferente contraseña if unique passwords son requerido per image."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:32
msgid ""
"Guest customizations are required when assigning static IP's manually or "
"using IP pools. They can be disabled per virtual image advanced settings "
"under |LibVir| > Edit Image > Advanced > Uncheck \"Force Guest "
"Customization\" if using DHCP. However the SID will not be changed from the "
"source template. In addition, new VM's will not be able to join a domain "
"that had already been joined by the source template or any other VM's with "
"that SID."
msgstr ""
"Guest customizations son requerido cuando assigning static IP's manualmente "
"o using IP pools. They se puede deshabilitar per virtual image advanced "
"configuración under |LibVir| > Edit Image > Advanced > Uncheck \"Force Guest"
" Customization\" if using DHCP. Sin embargo el SID no be cambiado desde el "
"origen template. Además, nuevo VM's no be able to join un domain que tenía "
"ya sido joined by el origen template o cualquier otro VM's con que SID."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:35
msgid "Existing Instances"
msgstr "Existing Instances"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:37
msgid ""
"|morpheus| provides several features regarding pulling in existing virtual "
"machines and servers in an environment. Most cloud options contain a "
"checkbox titled '*Inventory Existing Instances*'. When this option is "
"selected, all VMs found within the specified scope of the cloud integration "
"will be scanned periodically and Virtual Machines will be synced into "
"|morpheus|. Users may also choose to onboard only virtual machines that are "
"running within specific Resource Pools. Once the vCenter Cloud is "
"integrated, navigate to the detail page for the specific Cloud (select it "
"from the list at |InfClo|). From the Resources tab, locate the Pools "
"section. Click ACTIONS > Edit next to a selected Resource Pool. If INVENTORY"
" is checked, |morpheus| will automatically onboard virtual machines from "
"that Resource Pool."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| provides several características regarding pulling in existente "
"virtual machines y servers in un entorno. Most cloud opciones contain un "
"casilla de verificación titled '*Inventory Existing Instances*'. When este "
"opción es seleccionado, todos VMs found dentro de el especificado scope of "
"la nube integration será be scanned periodically y Virtual Machines será be "
"synced en |morpheus|. Users puede también choose to onboard solo virtual "
"machines que son running dentro de específico Resource Pools. Once el "
"vCenter Cloud es integrated, navigate to el página de detalles para el "
"específico Cloud (select it desde el lista at |InfClo|). Desde el Resources "
"pestaña, locate el Pools sección. Click ACTIONS > Edit siguiente to un "
"seleccionado Resource Pool. If INVENTORY es checked, |morpheus| será "
"automáticamente onboard virtual machines desde que Resource Pool."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:39
msgid ""
"By default these virtual machines are considered 'unmanaged' and do not "
"appear in the |ProIns| area but rather ``Infrastructure > Compute > Virtual "
"Machines``. However, a few features are provided with regards to unmanaged "
"instances. They can be assigned to various accounts if using a multitenant "
"master account, however it may be best suited to instead assign the "
"'Resource Pool' to an account and optionally move all servers with regards "
"to that pool (more on this later)."
msgstr ""
"By predeterminado estos virtual machines son considered 'unmanaged' y no "
"appear in el |ProIns| area pero rather ``Infrastructure > Compute > Virtual "
"Machines``. Sin embargo, un few características son provided con regards to "
"unmanaged instances. They puede be assigned to various accounts if using un "
"multitenant master cuenta, sin embargo it puede be best suited to en cambio "
"assign el 'Resource Pool' to un cuenta y opcionalmente move todos servers "
"con regards to que pool (más on este later)."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:41
msgid ""
"A server can also be made into a managed server. During this process remote "
"access is requested and an agent install is performed on the guest operating"
" system. This allows for guest operations regarding log acquisition and "
"stats. If the agent install fails, a server will still be marked as managed "
"and an Instance will be created in `Provisioning`, however certain features "
"will not function. This includes stats collection and logs."
msgstr ""
"A server puede también be made en un managed server. During este proceso "
"remoto acceso es requested y un agente install es performed on el guest "
"operating sistema. This allows para guest operaciones regarding log "
"acquisition y stats. If el agente install fails, un servidor será aún be "
"marked as managed y un Instance será creado in `Provisioning`, sin embargo "
"certain características no función. This includes stats collection y logs."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:43
msgid ""
"All Cloud data is resynchronized on a 5 minute interval. This includes "
"Datastores, Resource Pools, Networks, Blueprints, and Virtual Machines."
msgstr ""
"All Cloud datos es resynchronized on un 5 minute interval. This includes "
"Datastores, Resource Pools, Networks, Blueprints, y Virtual Machines."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:46
msgid "Service Plans"
msgstr "Planes de servicio"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:48
msgid ""
"A default set of Service Plans are created in |morpheus| for the VMware "
"provisioning engine. These Service Plans can be considered akin to AWS "
"Flavors or Openstack Flavors. They provide a means to set predefined tiers "
"on memory, storage, cores, and cpu. Price tables can also be applied to "
"these so estimated cost per virtual machine can be tracked as well as "
"pricing for customers. By default, these options are fixed sizes but can be "
"configured for dynamic sizing. A service plan can be configured to allow a "
"custom user entry for memory, storage, or cpu. To configure this, simply "
"edit an existing Service Plan tied to VMware or create a new one. These all "
"can be easily managed from the ``Admin > Plans & Pricing`` section."
msgstr ""
"A predeterminado set of Service Plans son creado in |morpheus| para el "
"VMware provisioning engine. These Service Plans puede be considered akin to "
"AWS Flavors o Openstack Flavors. They provide un means to set predefined "
"tiers on memory, storage, cores, y cpu. Price tables puede también be "
"applied to estos so estimated cost per virtual machine puede be tracked así "
"como pricing para customers. By predeterminado, estos opciones son fixed "
"sizes pero se puede configurar para dynamic sizing. A servicio plan se puede"
" configurar to allow un personalizado user entry para memory, storage, o "
"cpu. To configure este, simply edit un existente Service Plan tied to VMware"
" o create un nuevo one. These todos puede be easily managed desde el ``Admin"
" > Plans & Pricing`` sección."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:51
msgid "Virtual Images / Blueprints"
msgstr "Virtual Images / Blueprints"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:53
msgid ""
"|morpheus| will automatically take an inventory of all blueprints configured"
" in vCenter and present them as options during provisioning. However, in "
"order for |morpheus| to properly provision these virtual machines and "
"provide accurate stats and health of these virtual machines, an agent must "
"be installed during virtual machine startup. This means remote access needs "
"to be granted at the guest operating system level to |morpheus| . To "
"properly configure these virtual images, find the relevant images in "
"|LibVir| and edit the entry. On this form, a few options are presented. The "
"first is a check box asking whether or not cloud-init is enabled. If cloud-"
"init is enabled, simply provide the default OS username configured (for "
"Ubuntu the username is `ubuntu` and for CentOS the username is `centos`). "
"For those looking to add cloud-init to existing blueprints |morpheus| "
"requires no special configuration and can use the default `cloud.cfg` "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| será automáticamente take un inventory of todos blueprints "
"configurado in vCenter y present them as opciones durante provisioning. Sin "
"embargo, in order para |morpheus| to properly provision estos virtual "
"machines y provide accurate stats y health of estos virtual machines, un "
"agente debe estar instalado durante virtual machine startup. This means "
"remoto acceso necesita ser granted at el guest operating sistema level to "
"|morpheus| . To properly configure estos virtual images, find el relevante "
"images in |LibVir| y edit el entry. On este formulario, un few opciones son "
"presented. The primero es un casilla de verificación asking whether o no "
"cloud-init es habilitado. If cloud-init es habilitado, simply provide el "
"predeterminado OS nombre de usuario configurado (para Ubuntu el usuarioname "
"es `ubuntu` y para CentOS el usuarioname es `centos`). For esos looking to "
"add cloud-init to existente blueprints |morpheus| requires no special "
"configuración y puede use el predeterminado `cloud.cfg` configuración."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:55
msgid ""
"A global cloud-init username/password can also be configured per account as "
"well as a keypair via the ``Admin->Provisioning`` settings section. The "
"great benefit of utilizing cloud-init is default blueprints do not need "
"common credential sets thereby increasing provisioning security."
msgstr ""
"A global cloud-init nombre de usuario/contraseña puede también be "
"configurado per cuenta así como un keypair via el ``Admin->Provisioning`` "
"configuración sección. The great benefit of utilizing cloud-init es "
"predeterminado blueprints no need common credential sets thereby increasing "
"provisioning security."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:57
msgid ""
"Windows systems do not typically support cloud-init. So simply turn this "
"checkbox off and provide the `Administrator` credentials. It should be noted"
" that these credentials are encrypted in the database. If using WinRM for "
"the RPC Mode instead of VMware tools, a Local or Domain Administrator "
"account credential set can be provided instead."
msgstr ""
"Windows systems no típicamente support cloud-init. So simply turn este "
"casilla de verificación off y provide el `Administrator` credentials. It "
"debería be noted que estos credentials son encrypted in el database. If "
"using WinRM para el RPC Mode en cambio of VMware tools, un Local o Domain "
"Administrator cuenta credential set puede be provided en cambio."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:60
msgid "Snapshots"
msgstr "Snapshots"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:62
msgid ""
"|morpheus| allows the ability to create a snapshot of a VM in VMware "
"vCenter.  From the instance detail page, simply select ``Actions > Create "
"Snapshot`` to begin creation of a new Snapshot.  Existing snapshots can be "
"viewed in the ``BACKUPS`` tab on the instance detail page.  Snapshots taken "
"in vCenter will sync into |morpheus| every five minutes.  To revert to a "
"previous snapshot, click on the revert icon located on the right side of the"
" Snapshot. Snapshots can be deleted by clicking on the trash can icon."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| allows el ability to create un snapshot of un VM in VMware "
"vCenter.  Desde el instance página de detalles, simply select ``Actions > "
"Create Snapshot`` to begin creation of un nuevo Snapshot.  Existing "
"snapshots se puede ver in el ``BACKUPS`` pestaña on la instancia página de "
"detalles.  Snapshots taken in vCenter será sync en |morpheus| cada five "
"minutes.  To revert to un anterior snapshot, click on el revert icon located"
" un la derecha side of el Snapshot. Snapshots se puede eliminar by clicking "
"on el trash puede icon."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:64
msgid ""
"Access to Snapshots can be limited or removed entirely for specific user "
"roles as needed. To edit a role's Snapshots permissions, go to |AdmRol| > "
"(Your selected role) > Snapshots. Users can be given Full, Read-only, or No "
"access."
msgstr ""
"Access to Snapshots puede be limited o eliminado entirely para específico "
"user roles según sea necesario. To edit un rol's Snapshots permisos, go to "
"|AdmRol| > (Your seleccionado role) > Snapshots. Users puede be given Full, "
"Read-solo, o No acceso."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:66
msgid ""
"|morpheus| supports the use of SR-IOV network adapters with VMware Clouds. "
"Bear in mind that VMware does not support Snapshots for this network adapter"
" type and for that reason Snapshot and backup-related features will also "
"fail in |morpheus| for VMs using SR-IOV network adapters."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| supports el use of SR-IOV network adapters con VMware Clouds. "
"Bear in mind que VMware no soporta Snapshots para esta red adapter tipo y "
"para que reason Snapshot y backup-related características será también fail "
"in |morpheus| para VMs using SR-IOV network adapters."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:69
msgid "Affinity Groups"
msgstr "Affinity Groups"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:71
msgid ""
"|morpheus| offers two-way sync for affinity groups with integrated VMware "
"vCenter Clouds. An affinity group contains a type (either Keep Together or "
"Keep Separate) and a list of servers which should have the rule applied. "
"Affinity groups created from |morpheus| create \"Should\" rules (soft rules)"
" rather than \"Must\" rules (hard rules) in vCenter. Thus whenever possible,"
" servers configured to \"Keep Together\" will run on the same cluster host "
"while servers configured to \"Keep Separate\" will be balanced across "
"cluster hosts to the maximum extent possible. These rules may be broken if "
"necessary to balance resources or recover from failures."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| offers two-way sync para affinity groups con integrated VMware "
"vCenter Clouds. An affinity group contains un tipo (either Keep Together o "
"Keep Separate) y un lista of servers cual debería tienen el rule applied. "
"Affinity groups creado desde |morpheus| create \"Should\" rules (soft rules)"
" rather than \"Must\" rules (hard rules) in vCenter. Thus whenever possible,"
" servers configurado to \"Keep Together\" será run on el mismo cluster host "
"mientras servers configurado to \"Keep Separate\" será be balanced across "
"cluster hosts to el máximo extent possible. These rules puede be broken si "
"es necesario to balance recursos o recover desde failures."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:73
msgid ""
"It is possible to create an empty affinity group (that is, one with no "
"servers selected) in |morpheus| even though this is not possible in vCenter."
" If such an affinity group is created, |morpheus| will hold it without "
"syncing to vCenter until at least one server is added and the affinity group"
" becomes compatible with the vCenter API."
msgstr ""
"It es possible to create un vacío affinity group (que es, one con no servers"
" seleccionado) in |morpheus| incluso though este no es possible in vCenter. "
"If such un affinity group es creado, |morpheus| será hold it sin syncing to "
"vCenter hasta at least one server es agregado y el affinity group becomes "
"compatible con el vCenter API."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:76
msgid "Viewing Affinity Groups"
msgstr "Viewing Affinity Groups"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:78
msgid ""
"Affinity groups are listed on the Resources tab of the Cloud detail page "
"(|InfClo|, then select the appropriate VMware Cloud). From the ACTIONS menu "
"for each affinity group, they may be edited or deleted. By editing an "
"affinity group, users may view or edit its enabled status (affinity groups "
"which are not enabled will not be acted on)."
msgstr ""
"Affinity groups son listed on el Resources pestaña of el Cloud página de "
"detalles (|InfClo|, entonces select el apropiado VMware Cloud). Desde el "
"ACTIONS menú para cada affinity group, they puede be edited o eliminado. By "
"editing un affinity group, users puede view o edit its habilitado estado "
"(affinity groups cual no son habilitado no be acted on)."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:81
msgid "Adding Affinity Groups"
msgstr "Agregar Affinity Groups"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:83
msgid ""
"Affinity groups are listed on the Resources tab of the VMware Cloud detail "
"page (|InfClo|, then select the appropriate VMware Cloud). From here, to "
"create a new affinity group, click :guilabel:`+ ADD`. Configure the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"Affinity groups son listed on el Resources pestaña of el VMware Cloud página"
" de detalles (|InfClo|, entonces select el apropiado VMware Cloud). From "
"aquí, to create un nuevo affinity group, click :guilabel:`+ AGREGAR`. "
"Configure el following:"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:85
msgid "**NAME:** A name for the affinity group"
msgstr "**NAME:** A nombre para el affinity group"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:86
msgid ""
"**TYPE:** Select either \"Keep Together\" or \"Keep Separate\" to indicate "
"whether the selected servers should run on as few or as many servers as "
"possible within the capabilities of the HVM Cluster"
msgstr ""
"**TYPE:** Select either \"Keep Together\" o \"Keep Separate\" to indicate "
"whether el seleccionado servers debería run on as few o as muchos servers as"
" possible dentro de el capabilities of el HVM Cluster"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:87
msgid "**CLUSTER:** Select the vCenter cluster"
msgstr "**CLUSTER:** Seleccione el vCenter cluster"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:88
msgid ""
"**ACTIVE:** When checked, the rules defined in the affinity group will be "
"applied to the HVM Cluster"
msgstr ""
"**ACTIVE:** When checked, el rules definido in el affinity group será be "
"applied to el HVM Cluster"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:89
msgid "**SERVERS:** Select as many servers as desired from the typeahead list"
msgstr ""
"**SERVERS:** Select as muchos servers como se desee desde el typeahead lista"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:91
msgid ""
"Once finished, click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`. Following the next Cloud "
"sync, the affinity rule will be applied and VMs will begin to migrate (if "
"applicable)."
msgstr ""
"Once finished, click :guilabel:`GUARDAR CHANGES`. Following el siguiente "
"Cloud sync, el affinity rule será be applied y VMs será begin to migrate (si"
" corresponde)."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:94
msgid "Adding Servers to Affinity Groups at Provision Time"
msgstr "Agregar Servers to Affinity Groups at Provision Time"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:96
msgid ""
"In addition to adding servers from the affinity group, newly-provisioned "
"servers may be added to an affinity group at provision time. From the "
"CONFIGURE tab of the provisioning wizard, expand the Advanced Options "
"section. Within Advanced Options, select an affinity group. The affinity "
"group must be pre-existing and this list will be filtered to show only "
"affinity groups that apply depending on other configuration parameters set "
"on the new Instance."
msgstr ""
"Además to adding servers desde el affinity group, newly-provisioned servers "
"puede be agregado to un affinity group at provision time. Desde el CONFIGURE"
" pestaña of el provisioning wizard, expand el Advanced Options sección. "
"Within Advanced Options, select un affinity group. The affinity group debe "
"be pre-existente y este lista será be filtered to show solo affinity groups "
"que apply dependiendo de otro configuración parámetros set on el nuevo "
"Instance."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:99
msgid "Tagging and Metadata"
msgstr "Tagging y Metadata"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:101
msgid ""
"As of Morpheus version 4.1.0, tagging support is included for vCenter in "
"addition to the other clouds that have already supported it in past "
"versions. Tags will sync to vCenter from Morpheus and existing tags are also"
" inventoried from vCenter into Morpheus."
msgstr ""
"As of Morpheus versión 4.1.0, tagging support es incluido para vCenter "
"además to el otro clouds que tienen ya compatible it in past versions. Tags "
"será sync to vCenter desde Morpheus y existente tags son también inventoried"
" desde vCenter en Morpheus."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:103
msgid ""
"This feature requires a minimum API version of vCenter 6.5. The API version "
"can be edited by navigating to 'Infrastructure > Clouds' and clicking the "
"edit (pencil) button in the row for the relevant cloud. The field is labeled"
" 'VERSION'."
msgstr ""
"This característica requires un mínimo API versión of vCenter 6.5. The API "
"versión puede be edited by navigating to 'Infrastructure > Clouds' y "
"clicking el edit (pencil) botón in el row para el relevante cloud. The campo"
" es labeled 'VERSION'."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:105
msgid ""
"Tags can be created on-demand when provisioning from the 'CONFIGURE' tab of "
"the 'CREATE INSTANCE' wizard (|ProIns|). Within the 'Metadata' drawer, you "
"will see sets of fields to enter key/value pairs. On creation of the "
"instance, this metadata will be synced into vCenter."
msgstr ""
"Tags se puede crear on-demand cuando provisioning desde el 'CONFIGURE' "
"pestaña of el 'CREATE INSTANCE' wizard (|ProIns|). Within el 'Metadata' "
"drawer, you será see sets of campos to enter key/valor pairs. On creation of"
" la instancia, este metadata será be synced en vCenter."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/getting_started.rst:107
msgid ""
"'Inputs' from your library can also be exported as metadata for use with "
"vCenter. When adding or editing a new Input (|LibOptInp|), simply mark the "
"box labeled 'EXPORT AS METADATA'. The 'FIELD NAME' becomes the tag category "
"in VMWare."
msgstr ""
"'Inputs' desde your library puede también be exported as metadata para use "
"con vCenter. When adding o editing un nuevo Input (|LibOptInp|), simply mark"
" el box labeled 'EXPORT AS METADATA'. The 'FIELD NAME' becomes el tag "
"category in VMWare."

